"A","C","D","D","C","B","A","B","C","C","C","C","C","C","D","C","D","B","C","B","C","C","A","D","C","C","C","B","C","B","C","B","A","C","A","C","A","C","B","C"],"O":["Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Selected","Not Selected","Not Selected"],"P":["Yes","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","No","Yes","No","Yes","No","No","No"],"Q":["Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Hostel","Day Scholar","Day Scholar","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel","Hostel"]}$q$::jsonb;
 summary_formulas jsonb := $q${"T2":["=COUNTA(B2:B201)",200],"T3":["=COUNT(G2:G201)",183],"T4":["=COUNTIF(M2:M201,\"PASS\")",157],"T5":["=COUNTIF(C2:C201,\"F\")",82],"T6":["=COUNTIF(J2:J201,\">=35\")",44],"T7":["=COUNTIF(H2:H201,\"<40\")",39],"T8":["=COUNTIF(D2:D201,\"<>Jaipur\")",151],"T9":["=COUNTIFS(C2:C201,\"F\",M2:M201,\"PASS\")",62],"T10":["=COUNTIFS(E2:E201,\"OBC\",D2:D201,\"Kota\")",6],"T11":["=ROUND(AVERAGEIF(D2:D201,\"Jodhpur\",K2:K201),2)",213.24]}$q$::jsonb;
 questions jsonb := $q$[{"n":1,"marks":1,"text":"Make the heading row A1:Q1 Bold, give it Yellow fill colour and apply Wrap Text.","solution":"1. Select **A1:Q1** (click A1, hold Shift, click Q1).\n2. HOME → **Bold** (Ctrl+B).\n3. HOME → **Fill Color ▾** → Standard Colors → **Yellow**.\n4. HOME → **Wrap Text**.\n\nChecked: every heading cell A1 to Q1 is bold, yellow and wrapped.","criteria":[{"rule":"cells","range":"A1:Q1","props":{"bold":[true],"fillColor":["FFFF00"],"wrap":[true]}}]},{"n":2,"marks":1,"text":"In column K (Total) find the Total of Hindi, English, Computer and Rajasthan GK (F to I) for every student using the SUM function.","solution":"1. Click **K2** and type **=SUM(F2:I2)** → Enter (Rajnish Sharma: 78+64+91+70 = 303).\n2. Click K2 again and **double-click the fill handle** (small square at the bottom-right of the cell) to copy the formula down to **K201**.\n\nWhy SUM and not =F2+G2+H2+I2? Some students were absent in English (**AB**). The + sign gives **#VALUE!** when a cell has text, but SUM skips text, so Pooja Meena (row 3) gets 92+66+58 = 216.\n\nChecked: a formula in every cell K2:K201 with the right total.","criteria":[{"column":"K"}]},{"n":3,"marks":1,"text":"In column L (Percentage) find the percentage of every student. Each subject is out of 100, so the maximum total is 400 (Percentage = Total ÷ 400 × 100).","solution":"1. Click **L2** and type **=K2/400*100** → Enter (303 ÷ 400 × 100 = 75.75).\n2. Double-click the fill handle of L2 to fill down to **L201**.\n\n(=K2/400 with the **Percent Style** button (%) also counts: it shows 75.75%.)\n\nChecked: every percentage in L2:L201.","criteria":[{"column":"L","alsoFraction":true}]},{"n":4,"marks":2,"text":"In column M (Result) using IF function write \"PASS\" if the Total is 160 or more (>=160), otherwise write \"FAIL\".","solution":"IF checks a condition: **=IF(condition, value if TRUE, value if FALSE)**. Text answers go inside double quotes.\n1. Click **M2** and type **=IF(K2>=160,\"PASS\",\"FAIL\")** → Enter.\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **M201**.\n\nComparison signs in Excel: **>** greater than, **<** less than, **>=** greater than or equal, **<=** less than or equal, **=** equal, **<>** not equal.\n\nChecked: PASS/FAIL in every cell M2:M201 (capital or small letters both count).","criteria":[{"column":"M"}]},{"n":5,"marks":2,"text":"In column N (Grade) using nested IF give grade on Percentage: 75 or more = \"A\", 60 or more = \"B\", 40 or more = \"C\", below 40 = \"D\".","solution":"A nested IF puts one IF inside another. Excel checks from left to right and stops at the first TRUE condition, so start from the highest grade.\n1. Click **N2** and type:\n   **=IF(L2>=75,\"A\",IF(L2>=60,\"B\",IF(L2>=40,\"C\",\"D\")))** → Enter.\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **N201**.\n\nCount the brackets: 3 IFs need 3 closing brackets at the end.\n\n**IFS** does the same job: =IFS(L2>=75,\"A\",L2>=60,\"B\",L2>=40,\"C\",L2<40,\"D\"). But IFS exists only in Excel 2019 / 365. **The exam uses Excel 2013, where IFS gives #NAME?** — learn the nested IF.\n\nChecked: the grade in every cell N2:N201.","criteria":[{"column":"N"}]},{"n":6,"marks":2,"text":"In column O (Selection) using IF with AND write \"Selected\" if the Total is 160 or more AND Typing Speed is 25 WPM or more, otherwise \"Not Selected\".","solution":"AND is TRUE only when **every** condition is TRUE.\n1. Click **O2** and type **=IF(AND(K2>=160,J2>=25),\"Selected\",\"Not Selected\")** → Enter.\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **O201**.\n\nNote: && (used in programming) does not work in Excel. Excel uses the **AND( )** function.\n\nChecked: every cell O2:O201.","criteria":[{"column":"O"}]},{"n":7,"marks":2,"text":"In column P (Scholarship) using IF with OR write \"Yes\" if a student got 90 or more in Hindi OR 90 or more in Computer, otherwise \"No\".","solution":"OR is TRUE when **at least one** condition is TRUE.\n1. Click **P2** and type **=IF(OR(F2>=90,H2>=90),\"Yes\",\"No\")** → Enter (Rajnish: Computer 91 → Yes).\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **P201**.\n\nNote: | or || (OR in programming) does not work in Excel. Excel uses the **OR( )** function.\n\nChecked: every cell P2:P201.","criteria":[{"column":"P"}]},{"n":8,"marks":2,"text":"In column Q (Hostel) using IF write \"Hostel\" if the District is not Jaipur, otherwise \"Day Scholar\". Use the not equal to (<>) sign.","solution":"In Excel \"not equal to\" is written **<>**. The signs ! and != (from programming) do not work in Excel; = means equal.\n1. Click **Q2** and type **=IF(D2<>\"Jaipur\",\"Hostel\",\"Day Scholar\")** → Enter.\n2. Double-click the fill handle to fill down to **Q201**.\n\nSame answer another way: =IF(D2=\"Jaipur\",\"Day Scholar\",\"Hostel\"), or =IF(NOT(D2=\"Jaipur\"),\"Hostel\",\"Day Scholar\").\n\nChecked: every cell Q2:Q201.","criteria":[{"column":"Q"}]},{"n":9,"marks":2,"text":"In cell T2 find the total number of students using COUNTA on Student Name (B2:B201), and in cell T3 find how many students appeared in English using COUNT on G2:G201.","solution":"**COUNTA** counts every cell that is not empty (text and numbers). **COUNT** counts only cells with numbers.\n1. **T2**: =COUNTA(B2:B201) → 200.\n2. **T3**: =COUNT(G2:G201) → 183 (the 17 students marked AB are text, so COUNT leaves them out).\n\nAlso useful: **COUNTBLANK** counts empty cells.\n\nChecked: T2 and T3, both with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"T2","equals":200,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"T3","equals":183,"formula":true}]},{"n":10,"marks":2,"text":"Using COUNTIF, in cell T4 count the students whose Result is \"PASS\", and in cell T5 count the girl students (Gender = \"F\").","solution":"**=COUNTIF(range, criteria)** counts the cells of a range that meet one condition.\n1. **T4**: =COUNTIF(M2:M201,\"PASS\") → 157.\n2. **T5**: =COUNTIF(C2:C201,\"F\") → 82.\n\n(T4 also works as =COUNTIF(K2:K201,\">=160\").)\n\nChecked: T4 and T5, both with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"T4","equals":157,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"T5","equals":82,"formula":true}]},{"n":11,"marks":2,"text":"Using COUNTIF with signs, count in T6 the students with Typing Speed 35 or more (>=35), in T7 the students with Computer marks below 40 (<40), and in T8 the students not from Jaipur (<>).","solution":"In COUNTIF the sign and the number go together inside double quotes.\n1. **T6**: =COUNTIF(J2:J201,\">=35\") → 44.\n2. **T7**: =COUNTIF(H2:H201,\"<40\") → 39.\n3. **T8**: =COUNTIF(D2:D201,\"<>Jaipur\") → 151.\n\nChecked: T6, T7 and T8, all with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"T6","equals":44,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"T7","equals":39,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"T8","equals":151,"formula":true}]},{"n":12,"marks":2,"text":"Using COUNTIFS (more than one condition), count in T9 the girls (F) whose Result is PASS, and in T10 the OBC students from Kota district.","solution":"**=COUNTIFS(range1, criteria1, range2, criteria2, ...)** counts the rows that meet **all** the conditions. Every range must have the same size.\n1. **T9**: =COUNTIFS(C2:C201,\"F\",M2:M201,\"PASS\") → 62.\n2. **T10**: =COUNTIFS(E2:E201,\"OBC\",D2:D201,\"Kota\") → 6.\n\nCOUNTIFS, SUMIFS and AVERAGEIFS all work in Excel 2013.\n\nChecked: T9 and T10, both with formulas.","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"T9","equals":62,"formula":true},{"rule":"value","cell":"T10","equals":6,"formula":true}]},{"n":13,"marks":2,"text":"In cell T11 find the average Total (column K) of the students of Jodhpur district using AVERAGEIF, rounded to 2 decimal places with ROUND.","solution":"**=AVERAGEIF(range, criteria, average_range)** averages only the rows that meet the condition. **=ROUND(number, 2)** keeps 2 decimal places.\n1. Click **T11** and type **=ROUND(AVERAGEIF(D2:D201,\"Jodhpur\",K2:K201),2)** → Enter → 213.24.\n\nThe same pattern: =SUMIF(D2:D201,\"Jodhpur\",K2:K201) adds them up instead.\n\nChecked: T11 = 213.24 with a formula. (The Decrease Decimal button only changes how the number looks, not the value, so use ROUND.)","criteria":[{"rule":"value","cell":"T11","equals":213.24,"formula":true}]},{"n":14,"marks":1,"text":"Select M2:M201 and with Conditional Formatting highlight the cells equal to \"FAIL\" with Light Red Fill with Dark Red Text.","solution":"1. Select **M2:M201** (click M2, then press **Ctrl+Shift+↓**).\n2. HOME → **Conditional Formatting ▾** → **Highlight Cells Rules** → **Equal To...**\n3. Type **FAIL**, keep **Light Red Fill with Dark Red Text** → **OK**.\n\n(Highlight Cells Rules → Text that Contains... with FAIL also counts.)\n\nChecked: the rule on M2:M201.","criteria":[{"rule":"anyOf","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M2:M201","type":"equalTo","value":"FAIL","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M2:M201","type":"equalTo","value":"Fail","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M2:M201","type":"equalTo","value":"fail","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M2:M201","type":"textContains","value":"FAIL","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M2:M201","type":"textContains","value":"Fail","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M2:M201","type":"textContains","value":"fail","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M1:M201","type":"equalTo","value":"FAIL","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M1:M201","type":"equalTo","value":"Fail","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M1:M201","type":"equalTo","value":"fail","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M1:M201","type":"textContains","value":"FAIL","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M1:M201","type":"textContains","value":"Fail","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}},{"rule":"sheet","path":"conditionalFormats","includes":{"range":"M1:M201","type":"textContains","value":"fail","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}}]}]},{"n":15,"marks":1,"text":"Apply Filter to the complete table A1:Q201.","solution":"1. Click any cell of the table, for example **A1**.\n2. DATA → **Filter** (or HOME → Sort & Filter ▾ → Filter, or **Ctrl+Shift+L**). Arrow buttons appear in the heading row.\n\nDo this after the formula columns are filled, so the filter covers A1:Q201.\n\nChecked: a filter on the table.","criteria":[{"rule":"sheet","path":"filter","in":["A1:J201","A1:K201","A1:L201","A1:M201","A1:N201","A1:O201","A1:P201","A1:Q201"]}]}]$q$::jsonb;
 cells jsonb; model_cells jsonb; working jsonb; model jsonb;
begin
 if exists (select 1 from public.excel_efficiency_tests where slug = 'efficiency-test-4') then raise notice 'EXCEL EFFICIENCY TEST 4 already exists'; return; end if;

 select jsonb_object_agg(ref, cell) into cells from (
   select chr(65 + i) || '1' as ref, pg_temp.excel_cell(headers->i) as cell from generate_series(0, jsonb_array_length(headers) - 1) i
   union all select chr(65 + i) || (r + 2), pg_temp.excel_cell(students->r->i) from generate_series(0, jsonb_array_length(students) - 1) r, generate_series(0, 9) i
   union all select s->>0, pg_temp.excel_cell(s->1) from jsonb_array_elements(summary) s) x;
 working := jsonb_build_object('schemaVersion', 1, 'language', 'English', 'rows', 201, 'cols', 20, 'cells', cells);
 perform public.assert_excel_efficiency_working_matter(working);

 select cells || jsonb_object_agg(ref, cell) into model_cells from (
   select t.key || (r + 2) as ref, pg_temp.excel_cell(vals->t.key->r, replace(t.value, '#', (r + 2)::text)) as cell from jsonb_each_text(templates) t, generate_series(0, 199) r
   union all select key, pg_temp.excel_cell(value->1, value->>0) from jsonb_each(summary_formulas)) x;
 select model_cells || jsonb_object_agg(chr(65 + i) || '1', (model_cells->(chr(65 + i) || '1')) || '{"bold":true,"fillColor":"FFFF00","wrap":true}'::jsonb)
   into model_cells from generate_series(0, jsonb_array_length(headers) - 1) i;
 model := jsonb_build_object('schemaVersion', '3', 'rows', 201, 'cols', 20, 'cells', model_cells, 'merges', '[]'::jsonb,
   'sheet', $q${"name":"Sheet1","filter":"A1:Q201","filterHidden":{},"conditionalFormats":[{"range":"M2:M201","type":"equalTo","value":"FAIL","style":"lightRedDarkRed"}]}$q$::jsonb, 'operations', '[]'::jsonb, 'savedAt', '2026-11-08T00:00:00.000Z');
 perform public.assert_excel_efficiency_document_schema(model);

 insert into public.excel_efficiency_tests (slug, title, language, status, created_by, sequence, auto_publish_results)
 values ('efficiency-test-4', 'EFFICIENCY TEST 4', 'English', 'draft', admin_id, 4, true) returning id into t_id;
 insert into public.excel_efficiency_versions (test_id, version_number, title, language, description, instructions_markdown, question_count, maximum_marks,
   duration_options, passing_marks, working_matter_snapshot, created_by, delivery_pdf, delivery_onscreen, student_question_toggle, model_answer_snapshot)
 values (t_id, 1, 'EFFICIENCY TEST 4', 'English', 'IF, nested IF, AND, OR, <>, COUNTA, COUNT, COUNTIF, COUNTIFS and AVERAGEIF on 200 students',
   $q$1. Carefully read the instructions and solve the questions accordingly.
2. All questions are mandatory.
3. The sheet has 200 students (rows 2 to 201). Fill a formula in row 2, then double-click the fill handle to copy it down to row 201.
4. **Maximum marks** and question-wise marks are shown with the questions.
5. Complete each task directly in the spreadsheet. Any method is fine (formula, drag and fill, Flash Fill or typing): the answer in the cells is what is checked.$q$, 15, 25, array[600, 900, 1200], 9, working, admin_id, false, true, true, model) returning id into v_id;
 update public.excel_efficiency_tests set current_version_id = v_id, current_version_number = 1 where id = t_id;

 for item in select value from jsonb_array_elements(questions) loop
  crit := '[]'::jsonb;
  for c in select value from jsonb_array_elements(item->'criteria') loop
   if not c ? 'column' then crit := crit || jsonb_build_array(c);
   elsif coalesce((c->>'alsoFraction')::boolean, false) then
    crit := crit || jsonb_build_array(jsonb_build_object('rule', 'anyOf', 'criteria', jsonb_build_array(
      jsonb_build_object('rule', 'allOf', 'criteria', pg_temp.column_checks(vals, c->>'column', 1)),
      jsonb_build_object('rule', 'allOf', 'criteria', pg_temp.column_checks(vals, c->>'column', 100)))));
   else crit := crit || pg_temp.column_checks(vals, c->>'column', 1);
   end if;
  end loop;
  insert into public.excel_efficiency_questions (version_id, question_number, instruction, marks, display_order, solution)
  values (v_id, (item->>'n')::int, item->>'text', (item->>'marks')::numeric, (item->>'n')::int, item->>'solution') returning id into q_id;
  insert into public.excel_efficiency_grading_rules (version_id, question_id, exact_target, expected_operation, expected_value, allocated_marks, additional_criteria)
  values (v_id, q_id, 'hand-written', 'rule-criteria', 'null'::jsonb, (item->>'marks')::numeric, crit);
 end loop;
end $mig$;

-- Check: the model answer scores the full marks of every question, the untouched sheet 0.
select q.question_number, q.marks,
  public.excel_efficiency_score_question(v.model_answer_snapshot, v.id, q.id, q.marks) as model,
  public.excel_efficiency_score_question(public.excel_efficiency_initial_editor_document(v.working_matter_snapshot), v.id, q.id, q.marks) as untouched
from public.excel_efficiency_tests t join public.excel_efficiency_versions v on v.id = t.current_version_id
join public.excel_efficiency_questions q on q.version_id = v.id where t.slug = 'efficiency-test-4' order by q.question_number;

commit;
